# Each call of the function that returns a class gets its own copy of the class, so A and B compile as if both parent classes were written out:
# `round` allocates both objects itself and calls every constructor, method and getter directly. Nothing is looked up by name.
# CHECK-LABEL: f1: size=
# CHECK-COUNT-8: function f
# CHECK-NOT: function f
# CHECK: stub AllocateCell.{{*}} x2
# CHECK-LABEL: f2: size=
# ONE-LABEL: f1: size=
# ONE-NOT: operation
# ONE-NOT: ById
# ONE-NOT: stub Call
# ONE-NOT: stub Construct
# ONE-NOT: stub ValueIs
# ONE-LABEL: f2: size=
